{
 "description": "Leave one mutant out: fit the wild type with tph-1 and tax-4, hold out pdfr-1 (description, discarded).\n\nFitted to wild-type behaviour alone, C.2's perturbation responses stayed undetermined in every fit,\nwith or without the inhibition and PDF constraints (`prototypes.py`). Here two of Scheer's mutants\njoin the objective, and the third is held out: does pdfr-1 then come out right without being fitted?\n\n- The model and constraints are V2's: the inhibitory scale floored at 0.09, PDF's strengths held\n  excitatory (PDFR-1 couples to Galpha-s).\n- The start is V2's last answer (its generation-90 readout: D 2.07).\n- The objective is v4's ranking score on the six families plus tph-1's and tax-4's two lawn\n  differences, each graded on its own 64-animal band against its wild type on the same animals and\n  entered as one more family: 1,000 x undefined + the root mean square over eight equal families of\n  10\u00b7asinh(z/10). Both guards apply.\n- The search: sep-CMA at population 24, sigma0 0.03, 64 animals a candidate, 60 generations on 16\n  workers.\n\nReadouts every 10 generations on the search's mean, on 200 animals (752,000,000 + i): every family\ngraded, mgl-1 against its wild type, and the three mutants. The stop rule, fixed before the run: at\ngeneration 30, stop unless each of tph-1 and tax-4 passes or its roaming z has come at least 1\ncloser to 0 than at generation 0. The branch, fixed before the run: if both fitted mutants pass at\nthe end with the readout D no more than 0.5 above its start, and pdfr-1 (held out) roams less and\npasses, a design around predicting held-out mutants is viable; otherwise the mutants are reported\nas unidentified.\n\nSeeds: fit animals 750,000,000 + 64\u00b7k + i; CMA 9485. Run from the repository root.\n",
